// ── LPADC1..2 ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Base/IRQ SOURCED from hw/arm/imxrt1180_soc.c:1093 (adc_cfg[]). These lived
// only in the motor and cm7 platforms, so every platform the SDK and Zephyr
// harnesses use had no ADC at all -- Zephyr's adc_api test printed 0 lines on
// Renode against QEMU's 10.
adc1: Analog.IMXRT1180_LPADC @ sysbus 0x42600000
    0 -> nvic@93

adc2: Analog.IMXRT1180_LPADC @ sysbus 0x42E00000
    // IRQ 189, SOURCED from imxrt1180_soc.h:194 (IMXRT1180_ADC2_IRQ). It was
    // written here as 94 -- inferred as "ADC1's 93, plus one", which is exactly
    // the fabrication this project forbids. The ADC IRQs are not adjacent: 93
    // and 189. Caught when m2 (which had the correct value) collided with this
    // one during the platform merge.
    0 -> nvic@189
